# Setup project

Configure this project without starting it or deleting data. This skill explains
destructive routes but never runs them. It is safe to invoke again whenever one
part of the configuration changes.

## Start by reading current state

1. Confirm that the repository root contains `.env`, `compose.yml`, and
   `backend/` before continuing.
2. Read `.env`. Report the current `FIRST_SUPERUSER` value and whether
   `FIRST_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD` is set. Show the generated `SECRET_KEY` and
   `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`; do not ask the user to replace either one.
3. State that `.env` and `.env*` are ignored by git, but values typed in a chat
   may still be retained in that conversation's transcript.
4. Offer the available setup sections and ask which ones to run:
   **Superuser**, **Email sending**, and **Error reporting**. Run only the
   sections the user chooses. For either of the latter two, follow
   [email-and-error-reporting.md](email-and-error-reporting.md).

